    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0668" n="1628" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1628"/>

                <head>No. 1107.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rives to Mavroyeni Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 3,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your note of the 30th ultimo, explaining that the recent regulations of the
                    Sublime Porte relative to the sojourn of Jews in Palestine are only applicable
                    to Israel ites emigrating in a body, and saying that no obstacle will be raised
                    against those who do not fall within this class.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L. Rives</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
